  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You already know what a heap is min heap gives you the smallest element in O(1), max heap gives you the largest. The two heap pattern uses&nbsp;<strong>both at the same time</strong>.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-problem-it-solves",
      "title": "1. The Problem It Solves",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Find the&nbsp;<strong>median</strong>&nbsp;of a stream of numbers as each new number arrives.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406367791-661399898.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We are given numbers one by one (like&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">5, 2, 8, 1, 9</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">) and after each insertion, we need to quickly find the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">median</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;(middle value).&nbsp;</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The challenge is that the data keeps growing, so we must update the answer efficiently every time a new number arrives.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The brute force way is to insert the number, sort the array again, and then pick the middle.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "But sorting every time takes&nbsp;<strong>O(n log n)</strong>&nbsp;per insertion, leading to&nbsp;<strong>O(n² log n)</strong>&nbsp;overall, which is too slow.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That’s why we need a better approach (using heaps) to maintain the median efficiently&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To find the&nbsp;<strong>median</strong>, it depends on how many numbers you have:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"></span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">If the count is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">odd</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;→ median is the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">middle element</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;(after sorting)</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">If the count is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">even</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;→ median is the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">average of two middle elements</strong><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-the-core-idea",
      "title": "2. The Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Split the numbers into two halves:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Left half → the smaller numbers → store in MAX heap</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Right half → the larger numbers → store in MIN heap</span>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Max heap gives top of left half (largest of small numbers)</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Min heap gives top of right half (smallest of large numbers)</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Median lives at the boundary between these two halves&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406367791-883683825.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><br></span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Numbers so far:&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">1, 2, 5, 8, 9</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Left half →&nbsp;<code>[2, 1]</code>&nbsp;(max heap → top = 2)<br>Right half →&nbsp;<code>[5, 8, 9]</code>&nbsp;(min heap → top = 5)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Max heap top = 2<br>Min heap top = 5",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Median =&nbsp;<code>(2 + 5) / 2 = 3.5</code>&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-the-balancing-rule",
      "title": "3. The Balancing Rule",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For the median to always be at the boundary, you must keep the two heaps&nbsp;<strong>balanced</strong>&nbsp; their sizes can differ by at most 1.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280987-132251181.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Allowed:</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "left size = right size → median = (left.top + right.top) / 2",
            "left size = right size + 1 → median = left.top",
            "right size = left size + 1 → median = right.top"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Not allowed:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "size difference greater than 1 (e.g., left = 5, right = 1) → heaps are unbalanced"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-how-insertion-works",
      "title": "4. How Insertion Works",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every new number goes through a two step process:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280987-216367358.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280987-216367358.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280987-216367358.png",
          "alt": "How Insertion Works"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Step 1:</b> Put the number in the correct half:<br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">If number ≤ max heap top → push to max heap (left half)</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">If number &gt; max heap top → push to min heap (right half)</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Step 2:</b> Rebalance if needed:<br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">If size difference &gt; 1 → move top from bigger heap to smaller heap</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Step by Step Example",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Insert numbers one by one:&nbsp;<code>5, 2, 8, 1, 9</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "<strong>Insert 5</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280988-811516386.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\"></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Push to max heap (default)</span><br></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Max:&nbsp;<code>[5]</code>, Min:&nbsp;<code>[]</code><br>Balanced → Median =&nbsp;<code>5</code></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Insert 2",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280988-47516341.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">2 ≤ 5 → push to max heap →&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 2]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Unbalanced → move 5 to min heap",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Max:&nbsp;<code>[2]</code>, Min:&nbsp;<code>[5]</code><br>Balanced → Median =&nbsp;<code>(2 + 5) / 2 = 3.5</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Insert 8",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406280988-82936148.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">8 &gt; 2 → push to min heap →&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 8]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Unbalanced → move 5 to max heap",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Max:&nbsp;<code>[5, 2]</code>, Min:&nbsp;<code>[8]</code><br>Balanced → Median =&nbsp;<code>5</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Insert 1",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460338-840061100.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">1 ≤ 5 → push to max heap →&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 2, 1]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Unbalanced → move 5 to min heap",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Max:&nbsp;<code>[2, 1]</code>, Min:&nbsp;<code>[5, 8]</code><br>Balanced → Median =&nbsp;<code>(2 + 5) / 2 = 3.5</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Insert 9",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460340-152260376.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">9 &gt; 2 → push to min heap →&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 8, 9]</code><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Unbalanced → move 5 to max heap",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Max:&nbsp;<code>[5, 2, 1]</code>, Min:&nbsp;<code>[8, 9]</code><br>Balanced → Median =&nbsp;<code>5</code>&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "class MedianFinder {\n\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> maxHeap;   // left half — smaller numbers\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> minHeap;   // right half — larger numbers\n\n    MedianFinder() {\n        maxHeap = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());\n        minHeap = new PriorityQueue<>();\n    }\n\n    void addNum(int num) {\n\n        // Step 1 — push to correct half\n        if (maxHeap.isEmpty() || num <= maxHeap.peek()) {\n            maxHeap.offer(num);\n        } else {\n            minHeap.offer(num);\n        }\n\n        // Step 2 — rebalance if needed\n        if (maxHeap.size() > minHeap.size() + 1) {\n            minHeap.offer(maxHeap.poll());\n        } else if (minHeap.size() > maxHeap.size() + 1) {\n            maxHeap.offer(minHeap.poll());\n        }\n    }\n\n    double getMedian() {\n        if (maxHeap.size() == minHeap.size()) {\n            return (maxHeap.peek() + minHeap.peek()) / 2.0;\n        } else if (maxHeap.size() > minHeap.size()) {\n            return maxHeap.peek();\n        } else {\n            return minHeap.peek();\n        }\n    }\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Complexity",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Insert</b>: O(log n) heap push / pop<br>Get median: O(1) just check tops<br><b>Space</b>: O(n) store all elements",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Beyond Median: Where Two Heaps Apply",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two heaps are useful whenever you need to maintain two groups and quickly access their boundary values.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "1. Sliding Window Median",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Find the median for every window of size K.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Array: [3, 1, 5, 2, 4], K = 3",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[3, 1, 5] → median = 3<br>[1, 5, 2] → median = 2<br>[5, 2, 4] → median = 4",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use the same two heaps, but now you also need to remove elements when they go out of the window.<br>Handle this using lazy deletion (mark and skip later).",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "2. IPO: Maximize Capital",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You are given projects with profit and required capital. Start with capital W and pick at most K projects to maximize final capital.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Projects: (1,0), (3,1), (5,2)<br>W = 0, K = 2",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Step 1 → With W = 0, only project (1,0) is possible → W = 1<br>Step 2 → With W = 1, projects (1,0) and (3,1) are possible → pick highest profit (3,1) → W = 4",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Final answer = 4",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6-two-heaps",
      "title": "6. Two heaps:",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406460340-178705676.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Min heap (by capital) → tells which projects are affordable right now</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Max heap (by profit) → among those, pick the highest profit</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At each <b>step</b>:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Move all affordable projects from min heap → max heap",
            "Pick top of max heap (max profit)",
            "Add profit to W",
            "Repeat K times&nbsp;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7-the-pattern-in-one-line-nbsp",
      "title": "7. The Pattern in One Line&nbsp;",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use&nbsp;<strong>two heaps</strong>&nbsp;when you need to split elements into&nbsp;<strong>two groups</strong>&nbsp;(usually smaller vs larger) and frequently query the&nbsp;<strong>boundary between them</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Max heap</strong>&nbsp;→ stores the lower half (smaller elements)<br>→ gives the&nbsp;<strong>largest element of the smaller group</strong>",
            "<strong>Min heap</strong>&nbsp;→ stores the upper half (larger elements)<br>→ gives the&nbsp;<strong>smallest element of the larger group</strong>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The&nbsp;<strong>boundary</strong>&nbsp;lies between these two tops, so you can access it in&nbsp;<strong>O(1)</strong>&nbsp;time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Or",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The two heap pattern is used when you need to divide elements into two groups, usually a smaller half and a larger half, and keep track of the boundary between them efficiently.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Instead of sorting everything again and again, you maintain just enough structure so that the important values are always easy to access.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A max heap stores the smaller half and gives you the largest value from that group, while a min heap stores the larger half and gives you the smallest value from that group.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The boundary (like the median) always lies between these two top elements, so you can get it in constant time while insertions remain efficient&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": []
}
